Date: Wed, 12 Aug 2026 08:30:00 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] NFC: nxp-nci: report the mode behind a failed read

Powering the controller fails with a -121 read after four interrupts arrive, and
the driver latches hard_fault on that error so every later interrupt is dropped.

Two things produce -EREMOTEIO here and they need telling apart: a read the
controller genuinely does not answer, and an interrupt that arrives while the
driver is still in NXP_NCI_MODE_COLD, where the handler returns -EREMOTEIO
without touching the bus at all.

Print the mode and the latch state alongside the error. Temporary bring-up aid.

Signed-off-by: Sr-0w <Sr-0w@users.noreply.github.com>
---
 drivers/nfc/nxp-nci/i2c.c | 5 +++++
 1 file changed, 5 insertions(+)

--- a/drivers/nfc/nxp-nci/i2c.c
+++ b/drivers/nfc/nxp-nci/i2c.c
@@ -225,6 +225,11 @@
 		break;
 	}
 
+	if (r < 0)
+		dev_info(&client->dev,
+			 "bring-up: irq read r=%d mode=%d hard_fault=%d\n",
+			 r, info->mode, phy->hard_fault);
+
 	if (r == -EREMOTEIO) {
 		phy->hard_fault = r;
 		if (info->mode == NXP_NCI_MODE_FW)
--
2.50.1
